# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15; board 1.54); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: three windows docked and one floating on the big display at a desk, a fifth on the laptop. The cable comes out. macOS brings
# the four windows over to the laptop by itself, and their apps say so. Arbor hears of displays only once they have settled, a second and
# a half later. Before that the person pauses Arbor (a pause lets go as a Quit does). Every window is in view, at its own size.
# Seen on a hosted Mac: all four went back to the display that was gone, and after a Quit nobody is left to fetch them.
# Spec: docs/features/F08-displays-and-spaces.md, docs/features/F40-pause.md. Window ids start at 101.
quiet
plug desk right 1920x1080
open Code 480x348
open Safari 480x348
open Terminal 480x348
open Chat 480x348
open Notes 480x348
move 101 1600 100 480 348
move 102 1700 150 480 348
move 103 1800 200 480 348
move 104 1900 250 480 348
cursor 2000 500
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
wait 5
loud
expect count docked 3
# The cable comes out.
quietly unplug desk
move 101 170 220 480 348
move 102 220 180 480 348
move 103 270 140 480 348
move 104 320 100 480 348
wait 1
pause
expect ok
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
expect visible 105
expect size 101 480x348
expect size 102 480x348
expect size 103 480x348
expect size 104 480x348
expect at 105 300 200
# And the pause ends like any other, on the one display there is.
wait 60
resume
expect ok
expect visible 101
expect visible 104
expect visible 105
# Back at the desk, the arrangement is too.
plug desk right 1920x1080
wait 3
expect count docked 3
expect left-of 101 102
expect above 102 103
